@model HTMX.Application.Web.Pages.Organizations.OrganizationFields
@using HTMX.Adapter.Customers.Contracts
@*
    The organization's Name field: its label, its input, the saved name when another save overtook this one, and its
    message. The fields card draws it, and the name check answers with it alone.

    When CheckNameAddress is set, HTMX checks the name as it is typed: 500 ms after the last key, and at once when the
    user leaves the field. A post from an input sends its whole form, the antiforgery token among them, so the handler
    binds and validates the name as the save does; it changes nothing, and answers 200 with this field. Each check
    replaces the one still running (hx-sync="this:replace"), so the newest name wins. Leaving the field sends one
    more, so a check sent before the last keys were typed never lands once the user has left.

    hx-swap="outerMorph" updates the field in place rather than replacing it: the input keeps the keyboard, its caret
    and whatever was typed after the check was sent, and only its error style and the message change. The message is
    a polite live region, so a screen reader reads it when it changes. The answer gives no control autofocus, so the
    keyboard stays wherever the user is by then.

    The check is advice: the save checks again, since another organization can take the name in between, and without
    HTMX the save is the only check. While the form shows another save's values the name is not checked, because the
    check's answer cannot know the saved name and would take it off the page.
*@
@{
    OrganizationInput input = Model.Input;
    OrganizationSingleResponse? saved = Model.Saved;
    string? savedName = saved is not null && saved.Name.Value != input.Name.Trim() ? saved.Name.Value : null;
    string? describedBy = savedName is null ? null : "name-saved";
    string? check = Model.CheckNameAddress;
}
<div class="field">
    <label asp-for="Input.Name"></label>
    @if (check is null)
    {
        <input asp-for="Input.Name" aria-describedby="@describedBy" />
    }
    else
    {
        <input asp-for="Input.Name" aria-describedby="@describedBy"
               hx-post="@check" hx-trigger="input changed delay:500ms, change"
               hx-target="closest .field" hx-swap="outerMorph" hx-sync="this:replace" />
    }
    @if (savedName is not null)
    {
        <p class="hint" id="name-saved">Saved as @savedName</p>
    }
    <span asp-validation-for="Input.Name" aria-live="@(check is null ? null : "polite")"></span>
</div>
